From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:45:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 075/159] [ae-patch] Dock the session rail whenever the chat
 keeps 480 px, and widen the sidebar's grab strip

The rail floated over the chat below a fixed 1280 px window width (1600 px with
the workspace panel open), whatever the sidebar was doing, so a window narrowed
to one side of the screen lost the right third of the chat even with the
sidebar closed. It now docks whenever the window, less the open sidebar, the
open workspace panel and its own 304 px, leaves the chat 480 px (the floor the
workspace panel already keeps), and floats only below that.

The sidebar already resizes from its right edge, but the 4 px strip was
invisible until hovered. It now takes 8 px and draws a line on hover and focus;
the session list moves 4 px in so its scrollbar stays clear of the strip.
